atlas surface

architecture scene-compiler
  canonical_name SceneCompiler
  family surface
  domain Surface / Scenes
  layer surface
  semantic_question Given whatever material a subject or route actually holds, which reading rhythms does that material itself argue for, in what order, and what should the page look like as a result?
  purpose The bridge between a large source estate and a page that feels like it. A route used to name its regions and a subject page used a fixed order, so adding thousands of sources and dozens of studied interaction grammars changed nothing a person saw. The compiler asks each declared rhythm whether the material argues for it -- one thing happening now makes a stage, several timed things make an agenda, three placed things make a map, pictures make a wall or a field, recordings that play make a tracklist, video makes a shelf, conversation makes threads -- and orders the ones that qualify by how strongly their own shape argues. The page is then dressed by the estate's own art direction: the material family its scene leads with chooses a family of Ghost presentation profile, and the subject's own address chooses which profile inside it, stably.
  maturity implemented
  consumes PageComposition
  consumes EventMaterial
  consumes PresentationTemplate
  publishes SceneSequence
  node_types SceneGrammar
  node_types SceneChoice
  invariant a rhythm appears only where the material argues for it: below its declared threshold the rhythm does not appear at all, so a thin subject stays thin instead of growing empty headings
  invariant on a route one material is read one way, and one region carries one rhythm: where two grammars argue for the same material or region, the stronger argument wins and the other is not shown
  invariant a detail page (a publisher's own address, an identity page, the relations of one piece) reads its material in depth: each rhythm consumes the stream in order while enough remains for its threshold -- lead, then index, then list -- every item is still read once, and one region still carries one rhythm
  invariant relations are material: the parts of a piece, the organizations it names and its publisher's channels are the passage, organization and channel streams, lowered through existing topologies (index, index, table) and chosen by the same thresholds as anything else
  invariant an event that has already finished argues for nothing: the compiler counts only what has not ended when it decides whether there is an agenda
  invariant the compiler chooses rhythms and nothing else: it cannot select a source, admit material, change a subject, invent a region or alter a word, and it returns a sequence of the same declared regions the executor already lowers
  invariant a route's own named regions still render, after the scene and without repeating a region the scene already read
  invariant a page's look is chosen by what it is made of and keyed by its own address, so the same subject always looks like itself; a profile carries ground, ink, accent, faces, measure and card treatment, and can change no word on the page
  forbidden_inference a chosen rhythm -> an editorial judgement about the material, or a ranking of the things inside it
  forbidden_inference a page's look -> a claim about its subject's importance, quality or standing
  forbidden_inference a scene -> a SurfaceScene closure with authority, actions or dependency tracking; this composes reading rhythms over retained material
  known_gap the thresholds are declared numbers, not measured ones: nothing yet checks whether a rhythm that appeared was worth appearing
  known_gap the compiler reads relation material only where a detail page builds it (item pages, publisher addresses, identity pages); subject rooms, people, places, events and topics are not yet relation streams
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/addressed_depth_test.sh proves an item page composes its parts, the organizations it links (resolved to their estate addresses, platforms left out) and its publisher's channels through the compiler, with no unrelated fill; page_programs, page_items, page_events and page_composition still pass, so routes keep one rhythm per material (2026-10-18)
  witness 2026-10-18 on a canary over a rebuilt subject projection: sib-swiss.aurekai.life composes broadsheet, index, cast, masthead and more from SIB's 22 kept pieces, 30 organizations named across its last 17 and its two channels, where the live address showed other publishers' events
  known_gap the look is chosen from the Ghost catalogue's colour and type tokens only; the estate's donor interaction grammars are not yet selected per scene
  source_path schemas/control/page-composition.cue
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tools/compile_page_composition.zig
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/page_composition_test.sh
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/page_events_test.sh
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/page_composition_test.sh and page_events_test.sh prove a composed route still renders its declared rhythms in reading order with one place to start listening, and that an identity page carries the pictures that depict it
  witness 2026-09-18 on the estate the same compiler produced materially different pages from the same code: /stage read as stage, map, tracklist, field, shelf and broadsheet under ghost-morning; /whats-on as stage, map and agenda under ghost-voice; /nearby as stage, map and field; /listen as a tracklist under ghost-neat; Dallas as wall, broadsheet, around and places -- none of those sequences is written down anywhere
  source_lineage 2026-09-18 the Rubicon: the material decides the page, instead of the page deciding the material

interaction scene-compiler-dresses-with-presentation-profiles
  source scene-compiler
  destination presentation-template
  relation chooses_profile_by_material
  preserves the profile's own tokens as the page's variables, and the subject's stable choice of profile
  drops every word, source and item of the subject; a profile sees only which material leads
  forbidden_inference a profile -> art direction anyone authored for that subject
  invalidates_on the published profile catalogue, the scene's leading material
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/page_composition_test.sh
